    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298">

                <pb facs="0700" n="586" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg586"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/8–1643: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Consul General at Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gascoigne</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the British Foreign Office
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d298-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-14">August 14,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>It seems obvious from what Signor Berio said last night that Badoglio, probably
                    in cooperation with the Germans, means to do all he can to play for time before
                    surrendering. Signor Berio earnestly stressed the German menace to Italy if the
                    present Italian Government showed signs of surrender and asked me what Badoglio
                    could do if the Germans were actually to start fighting Italian troops. The
                    Italians, lie said, could not successfully resist, and the situation would
                    become chaotic.</p>
                <pb facs="0701" n="587" xml:id="pg587"/>
                <list>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>May I have some information on the following points: <list>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                            <item>In what form should Badoglio’s unconditional surrender be made and
                                through what channel?</item>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                            <item>What military action should we take on receipt of such surrender?
                                i.e. should we be able, now that the Sicilian campaign is coming to
                                a close, immediately to land troops in Italy and assist Badoglio to
                                counter the Germans’ moves?</item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>I would propose to communicate your reply to (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >a</hi>) above to Signor Berio, while particulars asked for under (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">b</hi>) would be for my own information to assist me
                        with any future conversations which I may hold with Signor Berio. At the
                        same time I shall be most careful not to be drawn into a polemic and to say
                        anything to B. which you have not actually
                        authorized me to mention.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
